{"ts": "2026-11-21T09:07:08.155446Z", "run_id": "r-20261121T0829Z-500c", "unit": "openspec:add-visual-review", "seq": 43, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "Harness question: the pre_satisfied check could not discriminate because the unit adds only test files. The repository settles this: .l4/config.yaml lists **/*.test.* and e2e/** as test globs; tasks.md marks task 1.1 pre_satisfied and says the red step always stops on exactly this question, to be answered accept citing the T3 mutation rows; design.md and test-plan.md say the same. I read the held patch and checked the Node test's in-test mutations (J1, J2, J3) against the journey text and against the four page tables and 10-home.tsx: 13 required paths, the mutations each yield exactly one problem, every needle is present. The four imported conftest helpers exist. Nothing here needs a business decision; the accept only replays the patch through the normal gates.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1"], "target": null, "kind": "harness", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.4469124999999996, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "64df783dfaaec91a2a285a42e06cabe7f9cde15b49a616c8c3a82d0bb050b257", "checked": [{"ref": "spec:tasks.md", "quote": "both files are test files, so red writes them and the Node test is green when it is written", "claim": "The unit's task list declares task 1.1 pre_satisfied because both files are test files and tells the delegate to answer this harness question accept."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md#test-paths-and-the-red-step", "quote": "The Node test is green on arrival: tasks.md says `pre_satisfied` (R3).", "claim": "The design records that the Node test passes on arrival and that there is no production code for a green step."}, {"ref": "spec:test-plan.md#t3-rows-of-the-one-test", "quote": "The three mutated copies are what makes the test fail by assertion when a page, the CSP watch or the literal is dropped.", "claim": "The test plan says the test discriminates through its own mutation rows rather than through a production-code change."}, {"ref": ".l4/config.yaml:48", "quote": "- \"**/*.test.*\"", "claim": "web/src/visual-pages.test.ts matches the test globs, so the unit adds no production file and the zero-value run has nothing to vary."}, {"ref": "web/src/features/10-home.tsx:7", "quote": "navLabel: \"Home\",", "claim": "The home feature holds the literals requiredPaths looks for, so / is counted among the 13 required paths."}, {"ref": "web/src/admin/pages.ts:17", "quote": "path: \"/admin/users\",", "claim": "ADMIN_PAGES has four entries with non-null navLabel, contributing four required paths."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/pages.ts:22", "quote": "path: \"/admin/grants\",", "claim": "TOOL_PAGES has three entries including /admin/grants, so renaming it in the journey yields exactly the J1 problem."}, {"ref": "web/src/flows/pages.ts:22", "quote": "path: \"/flows/:flowId\",", "claim": "The flow-editor entry has navLabel null and adds nothing, so FLOW_PAGES contributes only /flows."}, {"ref": "web/src/runs/pages.ts:22", "quote": "path: \"/runs/:runId\",", "claim": "The run entry has navLabel null and adds nothing, so RUN_PAGES contributes only /runs, giving 13 required paths in total."}, {"ref": "e2e/conftest.py:149", "quote": "def watch_csp(page) -> list[str]:", "claim": "The conftest provides watch_csp, which the journey imports and calls once, so the J2 mutation removes exactly one needle."}]}
